      "id": "RKT-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "title": "Why the product of residue units acts freely",
      "anchor": "global-rank-orbit",
      "statement": "The compatible split level-zero forms yield a finite free model X for the product of the residue unit groups. Coordinate dilation is translation, and the coordinate norm is summation over that unit group. A tuple fixing a class belongs to the level and each of its multipliers is one.",
      "hypotheses": "Actual level prime T, level-zero tied forms, admissible stabilizers and the split local diamond data. The fixed-class argument uses the two distinct auxiliary type primes, trivial components there and the prime-to-characteristic local torsion result.",
