    {
      "id": "RKT-03",
      "chapter": "global",
      "title": "The lost rank as an exponentially decaying frame parameter",
      "anchor": "global-rank-share",
      "statement": "If T≥b^(m/2), b=exp(x^ε)≥3 and m≥2, then d_full−d_ram≤(2f/b)d_full. For each fixed admissible family one threshold suffices for all later x and all indices: choosing d_e=2f/b there gives sqrt(d_e)≤exp(−x^(ε/8)) uniformly over words. Using E_x=exp(−x^(ε/8)), the selected assembly promotes the cap to E_x² uniformly over indices, and the frame takes 5σ+3E_x.",
      "hypotheses": "Prime rank formula, TuSize and RamRankF, the family size bounds f≤k≤x^5 at the chosen scale, and positive ε. The full-rank-zero case uses the undivided inequality. The frame also needs independent matrix, geometry and lattice inputs.",
