      "statement": "Under the separated-gap hypotheses at a place, the change in log Vandermonde is at most 1/4+(2/3)k(1+log k). The normalization by fk after summing over f places yields logarithmic variation of the real level parameter; the global Count5 estimate compares the two prime windows and cancels their common auxiliary factor.",
